var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#MetidaFlows","page":"Home","text":"A lightweight experimental workflow engine for Julia\n\n\n\nMetidaFlows.jl is an early-stage project for building typed, graph-based execution workflows in Julia. It is currently under active development and not yet stable for production use.\n\nThe goal of the project is to explore how workflow systems can be expressed naturally using Julia’s type system and multiple dispatch, while keeping the core execution model explicit and minimal.\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows"},{"category":"section","location":"#Project-status","page":"Home","text":"This package is experimental.\n\nAPIs are subject to change without notice\ninternal execution semantics are still evolving\nsome subsystems are incomplete or in prototype state\nbackward compatibility is not guaranteed\n\nYou should expect breaking changes while the architecture stabilizes.\n\n","title":"⚠️ Project status"},{"category":"section","location":"#Core-idea","page":"Home","text":"A workflow in MetidaFlows consists of:\n\nNodes — units of computation\nPorts — typed inputs and outputs\nConnections — edges between ports\nSchedulers — execution strategies\n\nInstead of hidden execution magic, everything is explicit:\n\nexecution is driven by a scheduler\ndata is passed through typed ports\ninvalidation is propagated through the graph\n\n","title":"Core idea"},{"category":"section","location":"#Key-features-(current)","page":"Home","text":"Typed node system via Julia multiple dispatch\nDirected graph workflow model\nStrict connection validation (including type checking)\nTwo execution modes:\nDAW (deterministic DAG execution)\nABW (queue-based / agent-style execution, experimental)\nIncremental execution and invalidation propagation\nNode state tracking (:idle, :dirty, :clean, etc.)\nInput buffering system\nHooks for validation and execution lifecycle\nBasic serialization utilities\n\n","title":"Key features (current)"},{"category":"section","location":"#Minimal-example","page":"Home","text":"using MetidaFlows\nusing CSV, DataFrames\n\nstruct CSVNode <: AbstractNodeType end\nstruct DataFrameNode <: AbstractNodeType end\n\ncsv_spec = NodeSpec(\n    \"Load CSV\",\n    PortSpec[],\n    [PortSpec(\"CSV File\", CSV.File, :csv)],\n    [:file]\n)\n\ndf_spec = NodeSpec(\n    \"DataFrame\",\n    [PortSpec(\"CSV File\", CSV.File, :csv)],\n    [PortSpec(\"DataFrame\", DataFrame, :dataframe)]\n)\n\nfunction MetidaFlows.execute_unsafe!(node::DataNode{CSVNode})\n    csv = CSV.File(node.settings[:file])\n    setdata!(node, :csv, csv)\n    return [:csv]\nend\n\nfunction MetidaFlows.execute_unsafe!(node::DataNode{DataFrameNode})\n    csv = getinputdata(node, :csv)\n    setdata!(node, :dataframe, DataFrame(csv))\n    return [:dataframe]\nend\n\nworkflow = Workflow(0)\n\nid1 = add_node!(workflow, DataNode(CSVNode, csv_spec))\nid2 = add_node!(workflow, DataNode(DataFrameNode, df_spec))\n\nadd_connection!(workflow, id1, :csv, id2, :csv)\n\nsetsettings!(workflow, id1, Dict(:file => \"data.csv\"))\n\nscheduler!(workflow)\n\ndf = getdata(workflow, id2, :dataframe)\n\n","title":"Minimal example"},{"category":"section","location":"#Design-goals","page":"Home","text":"This project is guided by a few principles:\n\nexplicit execution model (no hidden state machines)\ncomposability via small typed primitives\nextensibility through multiple dispatch\nclear separation between:\nstructure (graph)\nexecution (scheduler)\nbehavior (nodes)\nsupport for both deterministic and dynamic workflows\n\n","title":"Design goals"},{"category":"section","location":"#Planned-direction","page":"Home","text":"The architecture is still evolving. Current exploration areas include:\n\nimproved logging and audit system\ncaching and checkpointing strategies\n\n","title":"Planned direction"},{"category":"section","location":"#Contributing-and-feedback","page":"Home","text":"Feedback is especially welcome on:\n\nexecution semantics\nscheduler design\ninvalidation model\nAPI ergonomics\nreal-world workflow use cases\n\nThe project is intentionally in an exploratory phase, so design discussions are highly valuable at this stage.\n\nDocumentation for MetidaFlows.\n\n","title":"Contributing & feedback"},{"category":"type","location":"#MetidaFlows.PortSpec","page":"Home","text":"PortSpec(name, datatype, label, ::T = SinglePort(); required::Bool = true) where T <: AbstractPortType\n\nSpecification of a node port.\n\nFields:\n\nname::String - human-readable name of the port.\ndatatype::Type - Julia type of the port data.\nlabel::Symbol - unique label used for referencing the port in code.\nrequired::Bool - whether the port is required for execution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.PortSpec"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.add_connection!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, MetidaFlows.NodeConnection}","page":"Home","text":"add_connection!(model::Workflow, c::NodeConnection)\n\nAdd connection to workflow.\n\nPerforms:\n\nconnection validation,\nconnection registration,\nincoming/outgoing index updates.\n\nIf the source node already has status :clean, its output data is immediately propagated into the target node input buffer.\n\nReturns\n\nAssigned connection identifier (Int).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.add_connection!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.add_node!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"add_node!(model::Workflow, node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nAdd node to workflow.\n\nAssigns a new unique node identifier and registers the node in workflow storage.\n\nReturns\n\nAssigned node identifier (Int).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.add_node!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.connection_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.NodeConnection}","page":"Home","text":"connection_to_dict(conn::NodeConnection) -> Dict\n\nConvert connection to dictionary representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.connection_to_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.delete_connection!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"delete_connection!(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nRemove connection from workflow.\n\nPerforms:\n\ndeletion of corresponding child input buffer entry,\nremoval from incoming/outgoing indices,\ndeletion from workflow connection storage.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if connection existed and was removed.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.delete_connection!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.delete_node!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"delete_node!(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nRemove node from workflow.\n\nPerforms:\n\ndeletion of all incoming and outgoing connections,\ncleanup of connection indices,\nremoval of node from workflow storage.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if node existed and was removed.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.delete_node!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.execute!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"execute!(model::Workflow, id::Int; execute_upstream::Bool = true, invalidate_downstream::Bool = true, check_cyclic::Bool = true)\n\nExecute workflow node.\n\nMain workflow execution entry point.\n\nExecution Stages\n\nInitialize per-run execution state and logs.\nOptionally detect recursive cyclic execution.\nSkip execution for nodes already marked :clean.\nMark node as :executing.\nOptionally execute upstream dependencies recursively.\nValidate node structure and execution readiness.\nValidate node settings.\nExecute node implementation via execute_unsafe!.\nStore execution state (ready_ports).\nPropagate outputs downstream through input buffers.\nOptionally invalidate downstream nodes.\nValidate execution result.\nMark node as :clean.\n\nArguments\n\nexecute_upstream: recursively execute all parent nodes before executing current node.\ninvalidate_downstream: invalidate downstream execution results after successful execution.\ncheck_cyclic: detect recursive execution loops during direct execution calls.\n\nReturns\n\nVector of output port labels (Vector{Symbol}) produced during execution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.execute!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.execute_unsafe!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"execute_unsafe!(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nLow-level node execution interface.\n\nThis function contains node-specific execution logic.\n\nThe default implementation throws an error and must be specialized for every executable node type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.execute_unsafe!"},{"category":"function","location":"#MetidaFlows.execution_node_validation","page":"Home","text":"execution_node_validation(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nInternal function. Validate node readiness before execution.\n\nChecks that:\n\nevery declared input port has a corresponding value in node.input_buffer,\nvalidate_node succeeds.\n\nThis validation is intended for runtime execution safety, ensuring that all required inputs are available before calling execute_unsafe!.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if node is ready for execution.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.execution_node_validation"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.find_connections-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"find_connections(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nReturn all connection IDs associated with a node (both incoming and outgoing).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.find_connections"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.get_children-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"get_children(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nGet children.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.get_children"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.get_parents-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"get_parents(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nReturn parents - id vector\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.get_parents"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getconnection-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getconnection(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nReturn connection by identifier id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getconnection"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getdata-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getdata(node::AbstractDataNode, l::Symbol)\n\nReturn output data stored under output port label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getdata"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getdata-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getdata(model::Workflow, id::Int, l::Symbol)\n\nReturn output data stored under output port label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getdata"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getid-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"getid(node::AbstractDataNode) -> Int\n\nReturn node unique identifier.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getid"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getinputdata-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getinputdata(node::AbstractDataNode, l::Symbol)\n\nRead value from node input buffer.\n\nDoes NOT consume or clear buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getinputdata"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getnode-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getnode(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nReturn node by identifier id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getnode"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getportconnections-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getportconnections(model::Workflow, id::Int, label::Symbol; direction = :both)\n\nReturn all connections attached to a specific port.\n\nDirection:\n\n:input\n:output\n:both\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getportconnections"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getportnumber-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getportnumber(node::AbstractDataNode, l::Symbol, direction::Symbol)\n\nReturn index of port by label and direction (:input or :output).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getportnumber"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getportspec-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getportspec(node::AbstractDataNode, l::Symbol, direction::Symbol)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getportspec"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getporttype-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Int64, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getporttype(node::AbstractDataNode, i::Int, direction::Symbol)\n\nReturn Julia datatype of port by index and direction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getporttype"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getporttype-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getporttype(node, label, direction) -> Type\n\nReturn Julia datatype of port by label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getporttype"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getposition-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"getposition(node::AbstractDataNode) -> Tuple{Int,Int}\n\nReturn node UI/graph position.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getposition"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getstate-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"getstate(node::AbstractDataNode, s::Symbol)\n\nGet value from node execution state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getstate"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.getstatus-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"getstatus(node::AbstractDataNode) -> Symbol\n\nReturn execution status of node.\n\nPossible values:\n\n:idle\n:dirty\n:clean\n:executing\n:failed\n:invalid_node\n:invalid_settings\n:invalid_result\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.getstatus"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.haveinputs-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"haveinputs(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nReturns true if node has at least one input port defined in its spec.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.haveinputs"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.invalidate_downstream!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"invalidate_downstream!(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nRecursively invalidate all downstream nodes.\n\nMarks the specified node and all descendant nodes as :dirty using mark_dirty!.\n\nThe traversal follows all outgoing connections recursively.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.invalidate_downstream!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.isnodeexist-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"isnodeexist(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.isnodeexist"},{"category":"function","location":"#MetidaFlows.isportexist","page":"Home","text":"isportexist(node::AbstractDataNode, port::Symbol, direction::Symbol = :any)\n\nCheck whether a port exists in node specification.\n\nDirection:\n\n:input\n:output\n:any\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.isportexist"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.isready-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"isready(model::Workflow, id::Int)\n\nCheck whether node is ready for execution.\n\nA node is considered ready when:\n\nall parent nodes connected through incoming edges have status :clean.\n\nNotes\n\nCurrent node status itself is not checked.\nInput buffer completeness is validated separately via execution_node_validation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.isready"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.mark_dirty!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"mark_dirty!(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nInvalidate node execution result.\n\nPerforms the following operations:\n\nsets node status to :dirty,\nclears ready_ports,\nclears cached output data stored in node.data.\n\nThis function intentionally does not clear:\n\nnode settings,\ninput buffer,\nexecution logs,\nexecution counters/state metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.mark_dirty!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.node_properties_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.NodeProperties}","page":"Home","text":"node_properties_to_dict(np::NodeProperties) -> Dict\n\nConvert node properties to JSON-serializable dictionary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.node_properties_to_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.node_schema-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"node_schema(node::AbstractDataNode) -> Dict\n\nDefault node schema.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.node_schema"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.node_schema_usermod!-Tuple{Any, MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"node_schema_usermod!(d, node::AbstractDataNode) -> Dict\n\nModify node schema for user-defined node types.\n\nPossible user modifications:\n\nnode_schema_usermod!(d, node::AbstractDataNode)\n    d[:section]   = \"Section 1\"\n    d[:groupname] = \"Group 1\"\n    d[:color]     = \"#8b5cf6\"\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.node_schema_usermod!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.node_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"node_to_dict(node::AbstractDataNode; specs::Bool = true) -> Dict\n\nConvert node to JSON-serializable dictionary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.node_to_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.portspec_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.PortSpec}","page":"Home","text":"portspec_to_dict(ps::PortSpec) -> Dict\n\nConvert PortSpec to dictionary representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.portspec_to_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.reset!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow}","page":"Home","text":"reset!(model::Workflow)\n\nReset workflow execution state.\n\nMarks every node in the workflow as :dirty using mark_dirty!, clears node execution state, and removes all cached output data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.reset!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.reset_status!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow}","page":"Home","text":"reset_status!(model::Workflow)\n\nReset only node statuses.\n\nSets status of every node in the workflow to :dirty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.reset_status!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.scheduler!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow{MetidaFlows.ABW}}","page":"Home","text":"scheduler!(model::Workflow{ABW}; maxiter = 1000)\n\nExecute workflow using queue-based agent/event scheduling.\n\nThis scheduler is intended for dynamic or agent-based workflows (ABW), where execution readiness is determined during runtime.\n\nArguments\n\nmaxiter: maximum number of scheduler iterations before aborting execution.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.scheduler!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.scheduler!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow{MetidaFlows.DAW}}","page":"Home","text":"scheduler!(model::Workflow{DAW})\n\nExecute entire data analysis workflow (DAW) using topological ordering.\n\nThis scheduler is designed for deterministic acyclic data-analysis workflows.\n\nExecution Steps\n\nBuild workflow graph.\nValidate graph acyclicity.\nGenerate new workflow run_id.\nReset node execution states.\nExecute nodes in topological order.\n\nNotes\n\nNodes are executed exactly once per scheduler run.\nUpstream execution and downstream invalidation are disabled because execution order is already guaranteed by topology.\nCyclic workflows are rejected before execution starts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.scheduler!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setdata!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Any}","page":"Home","text":"setdata!(node::AbstractDataNode, l::Symbol, d)\n\nStore output data in node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setdata!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setid!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"setid!(node::AbstractDataNode, id::Int) -> DataNode\n\nSet node identifier. Mutates node in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setid!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setinputbuffer!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Int64, Any}","page":"Home","text":"setinputbuffer!(node::AbstractDataNode, label::Symbol, connection_id::Int, value)\n\nWrite value into node input buffer.\n\nUsed by workflow engine to propagate outputs between nodes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setinputbuffer!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setposition!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Tuple{Int64, Int64}}","page":"Home","text":"setposition!(node::AbstractDataNode, p::Tuple{Int,Int}) -> DataNode\n\nSet UI/graph position of node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setposition!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setsettings!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow, Int64, Dict{Symbol}}","page":"Home","text":"setsettings!(model::Workflow, id::Int, settings::Dict{Symbol, <: Any})\n\nApply new node settings and invalidate dependent nodes.\n\nSettings are applied using setsettings_unsafe!, after which the target node and all downstream nodes are invalidated via invalidate_downstream!.\n\nNotes\n\nThis function is the safe high-level entry point for mutating node configuration inside a workflow.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setsettings!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setsettings_unsafe!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Dict{Symbol}}","page":"Home","text":"setsettings_unsafe!(node::AbstractDataNode, settings::Dict{Symbol, <: Any})\n\nDirect mutation of node settings without invalidation. Can be re-implemented for every node type.\n\nDefault implementation copies all provided key-value pairs into node.settings.\n\nWarning\n\nThis function does NOT invalidate cached execution results or downstream nodes.\n\nUse setsettings! for normal workflow operation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setsettings_unsafe!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setstate!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol, Any}","page":"Home","text":"setstate!(node::AbstractDataNode, s::Symbol, v) -> DataNode\n\nStore value in node execution state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setstate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.setstatus!-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode, Symbol}","page":"Home","text":"setstatus!(node::AbstractDataNode, s::Symbol) -> DataNode\n\nSet execution status of node.\n\nThis does NOT trigger validation or propagation. Pure mutation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.setstatus!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.settings_schema-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"settings_schema(node::AbstractDataNode) -> Dict\n\nDefault settings schema.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.settings_schema"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.settings_schema_usermod!-Tuple{Any, MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"settings_schema_usermod!(d, node::AbstractDataNode) -> Dict\n\nModify settings schema for user-defined node types.\n\nPossible user modifications:\n\nsettings_schema_usermod!(d, node::DataNode{MyNodeType})\n    settings_dict = Dict{Symbol, Any}()\n    settings_dict[:my_setting1] = Dict(:type => Int, \n        :default => 0, \n        :description => \"My setting 1\", \n        :required => true, \n        :pinned => true,\n        :source\t=> \"upstream\",\n        :validator => (x -> x >= 0))\n        \n    settings_dict[:my_setting2] = Dict(:type => Array{Int}, \n        :default => [0], \n        :description => \"My setting 2\", \n        :required => true, \n        :pinned => false,\n        :source\t=> \"none\",\n        :validator => (x -> x in [1,2,3]))\n    d[:schema] = settings_dict\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.settings_schema_usermod!"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.spec_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.NodeSpec}","page":"Home","text":"spec_to_dict(spec::NodeSpec) -> Dict\n\nConvert NodeSpec to dictionary representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.spec_to_dict"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.validate_node-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"validate_node(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nValidate node structure and configuration.\n\nDefault implementation always returns true.\n\nThis function is intended for specialization by concrete node implementations.\n\nTypical validation rules may include:\n\ninternal consistency checks,\nstructural constraints,\nnode-specific invariants.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if node structure is valid.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.validate_node"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.validate_result-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"validate_result(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nValidate node execution result.\n\nCalled after node execution completes.\n\nDefault implementation always returns true.\n\nThis function is intended for specialization by concrete node implementations.\n\nTypical validation rules may include:\n\noutput datatype verification,\nrequired output ports presence,\nshape or schema validation,\ndomain-specific consistency checks.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if execution result is valid.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.validate_result"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.validate_settings-Tuple{MetidaFlows.AbstractDataNode}","page":"Home","text":"validate_settings(node::AbstractDataNode)\n\nValidate node settings before execution.\n\nDefault implementation always returns true.\n\nThis function is intended for specialization by concrete node implementations.\n\nTypical validation rules may include:\n\nrequired setting presence,\nrange checks,\nsemantic validation of configuration values.\n\nReturns\n\ntrue if settings are valid.\nfalse otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.validate_settings"},{"category":"method","location":"#MetidaFlows.workflow_to_dict-Tuple{MetidaFlows.Workflow}","page":"Home","text":"workflow_to_dict(w::Workflow) -> Dict\n\nConvert workflow to dictionary representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MetidaFlows.workflow_to_dict"}]
}
